// QC: Better Immersion for Athkatla - Waukeen's Promenade
// Generated from original v76 English dialogue; translation reference @1..@23.
// Preserve references when adding new languages.

@1 = ~That was insane. I've never seen mages take anyone before. The whole building collapsed, just like that.~

@2 = ~You were there, weren't you? When the massacre took place and part of the promenade exploded. Whoever you are, I want nothing to do with you. You are suspicious.~

@3 = ~Watch out at night, folk. Vampires are tearing this place apart, fighting that god awful war with the opposing guild.~

@4 = ~Can you tell us more about it?~

@5 = ~Thanks for the warning.~

@6 = ~The city is crumbling, internally. Imagine we have a civil war of sorts, hiding in plain sight. Those bloodsuckers keep fighting Shadow Thieves, bodies keep piling up. I woke up to a female screaming bloody murder one night and found her body right on my doorstep. She was identified as a Shadow Thief. When will it end.~

@7 = ~What did I come here for? I wanted to see exotic animals, and they barely have any animals or beasts around here. Waste of time.~

@8 = ~Away from my cows! They don't like the touch of random vagabonds.~

@9 = ~Adventurers? Dungeon crawling and all? Visit Cromwell in Docks, he might have a perfect equipment for you.~

@10 = ~This leopard is a wonder of nature. Beautiful creatures such as this shouldn't be kept in cages.~

@11 = ~Truly sickening how drows are allowed in this town. Their presence here disrupts the natural order. These imbeciles should stay 15,000 feet underneath where they belong, and rot in there.~

@12 = ~I have no need for enemy's compliments. Begone, you dark-skinned fiend!~

@13 = ~Don't waste my time on idle chatter. I don't like your kind. Phi, adventurers. Coming in, taking what they want and leaving like dark clouds, never to come back.~

@14 = ~It is nice to meet you. I can tell you've been a lot recently, judging by the scars and dark bags underneath your eyes. You should immediately head to Mithrest Inn, in northern part of Waukeen Promenade. It's the coziest and most upscale inn in the whole city. Guaranteed.~

@15 = ~Me Zekiel. Me guarding these crates. Storekeep say I be good at my job.~

@16 = ~If you're new to the city, keep your eyes peeled. I have been robbed blind in the middle of the day, twice now. This city is plunging itself into muck every day.~

@17 = ~I can't stress enough how much I recommend you to leave this city. It's a vile place. Guild war, poverty, corruption and magic ban. But the best thing is, if you pay the government whatever they ask you to, you get a permit to cast spells within the city walls. They are making a buck of citizens to profit themselved, puny egoists.~

@18 = ~My house! The explosion at the promenade ruined my house! Look at it! If I ever get the piece of scum responsible I will rip the legs off their arse!~

@19 = ~I agree wholeheartedly.~

@20 = ~Foul language. I admit, I like you. You don't cower from saying what you believe. At least one thing elven folk can stun me with.~

@21 = ~Scrawny little kobold as a guard? What else? Dragon as a shopekeep?~

@22 = ~Ribald's prices are steeper than he claims they are. Girdle of strength cost more than I make, and I could use a muscle boost for cargo loading. How will I ever be able to afford it.~

@23 = ~I am responsible for keeping peace. Enjoy your drink and keep your weapons sheathed.~
